WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:03.269
-Our next guest is
a very funny actor and comedian

00:00:03.269 --> 00:00:04.804
you know from his work on
"Saturday Night Live."

00:00:04.804 --> 00:00:05.972
He stars in "Mr. Mayor,"

00:00:05.972 --> 00:00:08.575
which airs Tuesday nights
at 8:30 here on NBC.

00:00:08.575 --> 00:00:09.575
Let's take a look.

00:00:09.575 --> 00:00:11.577 line:0%
-Sir, I need your advice.
-Jayden...

00:00:11.577 --> 00:00:14.514
-My friend works at
the discotheque,

00:00:14.514 --> 00:00:16.949
but he just got invited to play
at the Olympics.

00:00:16.949 --> 00:00:19.519 line:0%
But the owner of
the discotheque is his husband,

00:00:19.519 --> 00:00:20.687 line:0%
and he's going to be
so mad at --

00:00:20.687 --> 00:00:21.788 line:0%
-Jayden. Jayden!

00:00:21.788 --> 00:00:23.389 line:0%
I'm on live TV right --

00:00:23.389 --> 00:00:25.058 line:0%
[ Chuckling ] Right now.

00:00:25.058 --> 00:00:26.692 line:0%
-Oh [bleep]
Did I say [bleep]

00:00:26.692 --> 00:00:28.094 line:0%
-No, no.
-I'm [bleep] sorry.

00:00:28.094 --> 00:00:29.629 line:0%
I'm sorry!
[Bleep] [Bleep]

00:00:29.629 --> 00:00:31.697 line:0%
[Bleep] [bleep] your [bleep]
I'm sorry!

00:00:31.697 --> 00:00:32.799 line:0%
-Now get out.
-[Bleep]

00:00:32.799 --> 00:00:34.801 line:0%
[ Door closes ]
-Oh, boy.

00:00:34.801 --> 00:00:38.938 line:0%
Where was I?
Um, I don't recall.

00:00:38.938 --> 00:00:41.841 line:0%
And neither should you,
Los Angeles.

00:00:41.841 --> 00:00:43.476 line:0%
-Please welcome back to the show

00:00:43.476 --> 00:00:46.279 line:0%
our very good friend
Bobby Moynihan!

00:00:46.279 --> 00:00:48.081
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:00:59.725 --> 00:01:01.694
Welcome back, my friend.

00:01:01.694 --> 00:01:03.129
-Hello! It's so good to see you.

00:01:03.129 --> 00:01:05.330
-It's so nice to have you back
in New York City for a few days.

00:01:05.330 --> 00:01:06.665
-Yes, it's wonderful.

00:01:06.665 --> 00:01:08.267
-Are you enjoying being back out
here on the East Coast?

00:01:08.267 --> 00:01:09.368
-It's weird to be back.

00:01:09.368 --> 00:01:10.436
I haven't been back in
like two years.

00:01:10.436 --> 00:01:11.537
-That's nuts.
-Very different.

00:01:11.537 --> 00:01:12.538
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:01:12.538 --> 00:01:13.572
-A lot's different.

00:01:13.572 --> 00:01:15.808
You've got --
Your daughter is 4.

00:01:15.808 --> 00:01:17.944
-Is she?
-Yeah.

00:01:17.944 --> 00:01:19.745
We did some --
We checked Wikipedia, yeah.

00:01:19.745 --> 00:01:21.313
-I got to check in with her.
Yeah, yeah.

00:01:21.313 --> 00:01:22.915
I hope she's doing well.

00:01:22.915 --> 00:01:24.283
No.

00:01:24.283 --> 00:01:26.018
Yeah, no, she's 4.
She's the best.

00:01:26.018 --> 00:01:27.253
-What's she into?

00:01:27.253 --> 00:01:29.655
-Everything that I am.
-Alright.

00:01:29.655 --> 00:01:31.190
I mean, you have --
I will say this.

00:01:31.190 --> 00:01:32.258
I say this lovingly.

00:01:32.258 --> 00:01:33.593
I feel like you have
a lot of tastes

00:01:33.593 --> 00:01:37.063
you were just waiting for a
child to share with you.

00:01:37.063 --> 00:01:39.732
-Correct. I realize what
I'm best at is

00:01:39.732 --> 00:01:41.234
playing with the toys.

00:01:41.234 --> 00:01:42.868
Yeah, a lot of trolls right now.

00:01:42.868 --> 00:01:45.271
A lot -- She, like,
had a little spooky phase.

00:01:45.271 --> 00:01:48.174
-Okay.
-A lot of monsters like Dracula.

00:01:48.174 --> 00:01:50.042
-Oh, that's fun to be
inside of that.

00:01:50.042 --> 00:01:53.580
-Yeah. What every little girl
loves -- mummies.

00:01:55.782 --> 00:01:58.351
She's the best.
-That's really exciting.

00:01:58.351 --> 00:02:00.019
And the
birthday's coming up, right?

00:02:00.019 --> 00:02:02.488
-Yes. Once a year.

00:02:02.488 --> 00:02:03.556
-Is that what they're doing now?

00:02:03.556 --> 00:02:05.091
Wow. Kids.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:02:05.091 --> 00:02:06.692
-Does she, like,
have any theme requests

00:02:06.692 --> 00:02:07.860
for her birthday or is...

00:02:07.860 --> 00:02:11.964
-Every year,
she asks for a theme request,

00:02:11.964 --> 00:02:14.100
and every year, it ends up being
"Toy Story" somehow.

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:16.602
I don't know why or how,
but it does.

00:02:16.602 --> 00:02:19.005
Maybe because
we don't buy new decorations.

00:02:20.606 --> 00:02:23.209
No, yeah, I think this year,
it's probably going --

00:02:23.209 --> 00:02:24.910
Right now,
very heavy into Sonic.

00:02:24.910 --> 00:02:26.746
Sonic and Knuckles right now.
-Oh, okay. Alright.

00:02:26.746 --> 00:02:27.913
Oh, that's exciting.

00:02:27.913 --> 00:02:29.549
-Yeah, it'll change
in like 14 hours.

00:02:29.549 --> 00:02:32.685
-You have a fantastic cast.
We saw Ted Danson in the clip.

00:02:32.685 --> 00:02:34.520
Holly Hunter, as well.
A couple of legends.

00:02:34.520 --> 00:02:36.288
-Yes. Yeah.

00:02:36.288 --> 00:02:37.957
-What are they like
to work with?

00:02:37.957 --> 00:02:39.958
-The best.

00:02:39.958 --> 00:02:44.097
I've learned so much about
acting from watching

00:02:44.097 --> 00:02:46.899
Holly Hunter for 40 seconds,
and from Ted Danson,

00:02:46.899 --> 00:02:48.067
I learned that you should have

00:02:48.067 --> 00:02:49.802
turkey and apples
like every hour.

00:02:49.802 --> 00:02:51.136
-Really?
-Yeah.

00:02:51.136 --> 00:02:54.273
-'Cause he looks outstanding.
He looks really good.

00:02:54.273 --> 00:02:56.275
-Yeah, he's a
really healthy man.

00:02:56.275 --> 00:02:58.477
-Yeah. And it's just
turkey and apples on the hour?

00:02:58.477 --> 00:03:03.149
-It's just 7 feet
filled with turkey and apples.

00:03:03.149 --> 00:03:04.583
-You got to eat a lot of turkey.

00:03:04.583 --> 00:03:05.951
Yeah, you don't want to go
higher than the -- Yeah.

00:03:05.951 --> 00:03:07.720
-You can't, you can't.
It'll come out the top.

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:10.290
-You do -- I know you're doing
a lot of V.O. stuff,

00:03:10.290 --> 00:03:12.158
and during the pandemic,
people who were smart

00:03:12.158 --> 00:03:14.093
built sort of
makeshift home studios.

00:03:14.093 --> 00:03:15.094
Did you do that?

00:03:15.094 --> 00:03:16.328
-Yes, almost instantly.

00:03:16.328 --> 00:03:17.530
-Okay.
-Yeah.

00:03:17.530 --> 00:03:20.033
The first V.O. job I got,
I said, "Can I keep this?

00:03:20.033 --> 00:03:21.668
Can I pay you
to keep all of this stuff?"

00:03:21.668 --> 00:03:22.735
-Because they sent you the gear.

00:03:22.735 --> 00:03:24.536
-Because they sent,
like, a setup

00:03:24.536 --> 00:03:25.972
and they said "yes," and I did.

00:03:25.972 --> 00:03:28.207
And I haven't -- I've been in
my closet for two years

00:03:28.207 --> 00:03:32.144
doing voices, like every other
45-year-old man.

00:03:33.111 --> 00:03:35.147
-You come out to play trolls
and then you go back in.

00:03:35.147 --> 00:03:36.849
-I play and then I go play
in the closet.

00:03:36.849 --> 00:03:38.350
Yeah, yeah.

00:03:38.350 --> 00:03:41.186
-You have a show you're doing
a voice on, "Lightning Wolves."

00:03:41.186 --> 00:03:42.388
-Yes. Yes.

00:03:42.388 --> 00:03:44.590
-So, explain "Lightning Wolves"
real quick.

00:03:44.590 --> 00:03:46.825
-"Lightning Wolves"
is a cartoon,

00:03:46.825 --> 00:03:49.095
a bunch of shorts that I wrote.

00:03:49.095 --> 00:03:51.764
It's based on --
loosely based on those, like,

00:03:51.764 --> 00:03:53.966
'80s cartoons --
"ThunderCats," "He-Man,"

00:03:53.966 --> 00:03:55.735
"Voltron," "G.I. Joe."

00:03:55.735 --> 00:03:58.304
And -- But this version is --

00:03:58.304 --> 00:04:01.207
You know, it was all about
teaching people life lessons

00:04:01.207 --> 00:04:03.008
or teaching
children life lessons,

00:04:03.008 --> 00:04:05.744
but it was really just there
to sell them toys.

00:04:05.744 --> 00:04:07.513
-Yeah.
-And that's what this is.

00:04:07.513 --> 00:04:11.717
It's just a bunch of
'80s characters realizing

00:04:11.717 --> 00:04:13.986
that they mean nothing
and they're just toys.

00:04:13.986 --> 00:04:17.857
-You also -- Welcome to
the children's-book-author game.

00:04:17.857 --> 00:04:19.558
-Yes, congratulations.
-Thank you very much, yeah.

00:04:19.558 --> 00:04:20.726
It's fun to write a kid's book.

00:04:20.726 --> 00:04:22.895
-I just read your
children's book

00:04:22.895 --> 00:04:24.297
to my daughter
and her whole class.

00:04:24.297 --> 00:04:26.398
-How'd it go?
-Not great.

00:04:26.398 --> 00:04:28.000
No, I'm just kidding!

00:04:28.734 --> 00:04:31.270
They didn't get it.
They were sad after I read it.

00:04:31.270 --> 00:04:34.040
-Oh, no!
That doesn't -- That's not good.

00:04:34.040 --> 00:04:36.142
-Two of the kids said, "I don't
want to do school anymore."

00:04:36.142 --> 00:04:38.377
-What?!
It made him stop wanting --

00:04:38.377 --> 00:04:40.412
-Yeah.
One said, "What's a bear?"

00:04:40.412 --> 00:04:41.647
-What's a bear?

00:04:41.647 --> 00:04:43.282
Well, they should probably go
back to school.

00:04:43.282 --> 00:04:44.350
-That kid's not great.

00:04:44.350 --> 00:04:46.218
-Should probably do
double school.

00:04:46.218 --> 00:04:48.053
-No, it went great.
I did your voice.

00:04:48.053 --> 00:04:49.688
-Oh, good.

00:04:49.688 --> 00:04:51.724
-It was great. It was fun.
It's so crazy.

00:04:51.724 --> 00:04:55.161
You will read my book
to my daughter's class soon.

00:04:55.161 --> 00:04:57.597
-Yes. And your book is called?

00:04:57.597 --> 00:04:59.064
-"Not All Sheep Are Boring!"

00:04:59.064 --> 00:05:00.533
-That's great.

00:05:00.533 --> 00:05:03.502
Is that the take, that a lot of
kids think sheep are boring?

00:05:03.502 --> 00:05:05.872
-Yeah. It's about a little toad
who says, you know,

00:05:05.872 --> 00:05:07.673
"People count sheep
to fall asleep,

00:05:07.673 --> 00:05:08.975
but not all sheep are boring.

00:05:08.975 --> 00:05:10.410
I can prove it."

00:05:10.410 --> 00:05:12.077
And, by the end,
you realize he's wrong.

00:05:12.077 --> 00:05:13.780
All sheep are boring.

00:05:15.248 --> 00:05:17.249
-And then -- and then the
butcher comes?

00:05:17.249 --> 00:05:21.186
-And then -- Yeah.
Kids need to learn.

00:05:22.120 --> 00:05:26.458
-Hey, so, you -- You've --
Again, I've known you

00:05:26.458 --> 00:05:28.294
to do animated voices
for a long time.

00:05:28.294 --> 00:05:29.795
You did one in our show,
"The Awesomes."

00:05:29.795 --> 00:05:31.463
-Yeah, I was
Teleportation Larry.

00:05:31.463 --> 00:05:32.698
-Yeah, a very famous,

00:05:32.698 --> 00:05:35.000
a very important character
to the canon.

00:05:35.000 --> 00:05:38.237
You also played a --
The Penguin in

00:05:38.237 --> 00:05:40.072
"Batman: The Audio Adventures."

00:05:40.072 --> 00:05:41.573
-Yeah, our
friend Dennis McNicholas.

00:05:41.573 --> 00:05:43.676
-Yep. I did a little voice work
in this, as well.

00:05:43.676 --> 00:05:46.078
The Penguin, though,
I couldn't help but notice,

00:05:46.078 --> 00:05:48.547
does feel to, like,
sort of complete the circle,

00:05:48.547 --> 00:05:51.183
because you played Danny DeVito
on the show a couple times.

00:05:51.183 --> 00:05:52.451
-Correct, yes.

00:05:52.451 --> 00:05:55.855
I was lucky enough when they let
me to play Danny DeVito.

00:05:55.855 --> 00:05:58.490
-Here's you and Taran as
George Clooney and Danny DeVito.

00:05:58.490 --> 00:06:00.393
-Aww, my Taran.

00:06:01.561 --> 00:06:02.962
-Yeah.

00:06:02.962 --> 00:06:05.831
Were you -- Are you pointing
'cause you were worried --

00:06:05.831 --> 00:06:07.766
-I just like tickling
this little guy.

00:06:07.766 --> 00:06:11.336
-I thought you were like that,
"Now, this one's me."

00:06:11.336 --> 00:06:13.773
-No, I just saw it and went,
"He's adorable!"

00:06:13.773 --> 00:06:15.741
-You also -- This
was "'Star Wars' Auditions,"

00:06:15.741 --> 00:06:19.178
and this was Danny DeVito
auditioning to play BB-8.

00:06:19.178 --> 00:06:20.546
-Yeah, that was all Colin Jost.

00:06:20.546 --> 00:06:21.980
Colin Jost was like,
"Would you mind dressing up as

00:06:21.980 --> 00:06:23.448
Danny DeVito
and just rolling around?"

00:06:23.448 --> 00:06:25.884
And I was like, "Yes."
I go, "Should I say anything?"

00:06:25.884 --> 00:06:28.888
And he goes, "When you're done,
just go, 'Right?'"

00:06:28.888 --> 00:06:30.222
-Perfect.
-That was all Jost.

00:06:30.222 --> 00:06:34.226
-And then you were lucky enough
to meet the legend,

00:06:34.226 --> 00:06:35.394
Mr. Danny DeVito.

00:06:35.394 --> 00:06:37.829
-Yeah. Right after I
played him on the show --

00:06:37.829 --> 00:06:39.598
I don't remember if it was
the "Star Wars" one

00:06:39.598 --> 00:06:42.534
or the Nespresso one,
but that night, like,

00:06:42.534 --> 00:06:45.938
directly after the show,
I had two of my buddies,

00:06:45.938 --> 00:06:47.940
Mike and Rob,
from high school, like, with me.

00:06:47.940 --> 00:06:49.375
Like, I had two buddies
from high school with me,

00:06:49.375 --> 00:06:51.144
because you want to look cool.

00:06:51.144 --> 00:06:52.745
And I get them to the party

00:06:52.745 --> 00:06:54.947
and we pull up to the party,
and it's the coolest.

00:06:54.947 --> 00:06:56.448
And you're on "SNL,"

00:06:56.448 --> 00:06:58.350
and your buddies
from high school are there.

00:06:58.350 --> 00:07:03.089
And I walk past a car
and I get, like, yanked like --

00:07:03.089 --> 00:07:04.523
And I'm like,
"I'm being assaulted,"

00:07:04.523 --> 00:07:05.691
and it's Danny DeVito.

00:07:05.691 --> 00:07:08.160
He's like, "You think it's funny
playing me?!"

00:07:08.160 --> 00:07:12.098
And he immediately let go
and was like, "I love you, kid."

00:07:12.098 --> 00:07:13.699
And I was like, "Well,
that was the greatest mo--

00:07:13.699 --> 00:07:15.735
I just got attacked by
Danny DeVito

00:07:15.735 --> 00:07:16.868
in front of my
high-school buddies."

00:07:16.868 --> 00:07:17.970
-I mean,
that's really the dream.

00:07:17.970 --> 00:07:21.173
-I've made it.

00:07:21.173 --> 00:07:24.443
-So, I was recently --
I was a guest on

00:07:24.443 --> 00:07:26.779
"The Tonight Show
with Jimmy Fallon" recently,

00:07:26.779 --> 00:07:28.314
and we were
talking about bombing.

00:07:28.314 --> 00:07:29.448
-Yeah.

00:07:29.448 --> 00:07:31.617
-Especially specifically
bombing at charity gigs.

00:07:31.617 --> 00:07:33.085
-Yes.

00:07:33.085 --> 00:07:35.688
-And I was talking -- And I
think you know where I'm going.

00:07:35.688 --> 00:07:37.990
-Yeah. Oh, no, I saw this. Yeah.

00:07:37.990 --> 00:07:39.925
-You and I together bombed worse

00:07:39.925 --> 00:07:41.527
than I've ever bombed
in my life.

00:07:41.527 --> 00:07:43.996
-It was...the worst.
-Yeah.

00:07:43.996 --> 00:07:45.030
-It was the absolute worst.

00:07:45.030 --> 00:07:46.899
-It was at
Madison Square Garden.

00:07:46.899 --> 00:07:48.033
-Madison Square Garden,

00:07:48.033 --> 00:07:50.069
the 12-12-12 Sandy concert,
benefit concert.

00:07:50.069 --> 00:07:51.303
-Yeah.

00:07:51.303 --> 00:07:53.505
-It had been going on for hours
at this point?

00:07:53.505 --> 00:07:57.610
-It was an incredible list
of bands and musicians.

00:07:57.610 --> 00:07:59.411
-Like a seven-hour concert,
I think.

00:07:59.411 --> 00:08:03.015
And we went on like
hour 5 1/2, 6?

00:08:03.015 --> 00:08:05.785
-Yep.
-You recounted it wrong.

00:08:05.785 --> 00:08:09.955
We went on after Kanye West...
-Okay.

00:08:09.955 --> 00:08:12.058
-...who was
in a kilt and screaming.

00:08:12.058 --> 00:08:13.225
-Yeah.

00:08:13.225 --> 00:08:15.327
-And then threw his mic
into the audience.

00:08:15.327 --> 00:08:16.995
And then when --
And then Chris Rock went,

00:08:16.995 --> 00:08:18.030
"Are you going out there?"

00:08:18.030 --> 00:08:19.832
-Yeah.
-And I was like, "Yeah."

00:08:19.832 --> 00:08:21.400
He's like, "In that costume?"

00:08:21.400 --> 00:08:23.001
-Now, we should note that
Bobby and I --

00:08:23.001 --> 00:08:26.538
what we did at the hurricane --
a concert for Hurricane Sandy,

00:08:26.538 --> 00:08:30.308
which was all music --
Arcade Fire, The Who, Kanye --

00:08:30.308 --> 00:08:33.912
-We went in between
Kanye West and Billy Joel.

00:08:33.912 --> 00:08:37.750
-Yeah. So imagine
you've just seen --

00:08:37.750 --> 00:08:39.719
You've just seen Kanye West.

00:08:39.719 --> 00:08:42.321
You see them roll out
Billy Joel's piano.

00:08:42.321 --> 00:08:44.123
Before that...
-But before that...

00:08:44.123 --> 00:08:48.394
-...I walk out as me,
and he walks out as Drunk Uncle.

00:08:48.394 --> 00:08:50.496
-Yeah, in costume,
which, by the way,

00:08:50.496 --> 00:08:52.831
they made me wear to
Madison Square Garden.

00:08:52.831 --> 00:08:54.199
I said, "Can I get dressed
when I get there?"

00:08:54.199 --> 00:08:55.401
They said,
"There's nowhere to dress."

00:08:55.401 --> 00:08:58.971
I said,
"Inside that tiny building?"

00:08:58.971 --> 00:09:02.274
So, I showed up in costume
and sat in a room

00:09:02.274 --> 00:09:05.577
with The Rolling Stones
in a wig.

00:09:05.577 --> 00:09:07.680
-And I -- Well, 'cause
the thing Chris Rock said

00:09:07.680 --> 00:09:09.181
that I remember is, he goes,

00:09:09.181 --> 00:09:12.084
"You're going to go
do sketches?"

00:09:12.084 --> 00:09:13.118
Because he knew.

00:09:13.118 --> 00:09:14.553
-He said,
"Are you in a costume?"

00:09:14.553 --> 00:09:18.157
I was like,
"I'm not that terrible, please."

00:09:18.157 --> 00:09:22.127
And we went out there,
and the second we got there,

00:09:22.127 --> 00:09:23.896
everyone got up to get a beer.

00:09:23.896 --> 00:09:26.365
-Yeah. It was amazing,
because I do feel like

00:09:26.365 --> 00:09:30.202
we were doing
Drunk Uncle for maybe

00:09:30.202 --> 00:09:33.139
the biggest collection of
drunk uncles

00:09:33.139 --> 00:09:35.307
that had ever been -- Yeah.

00:09:35.307 --> 00:09:37.109
-It was -- Do you know
what happened after that?

00:09:37.109 --> 00:09:39.778
-No, what happened after that?
-I...left.

00:09:39.778 --> 00:09:42.681
-Okay. You just went home.

00:09:42.681 --> 00:09:45.984
-I walked out and I didn't go
to the greenroom.

00:09:45.984 --> 00:09:47.953
I walked through
Madison Square Garden.

00:09:47.953 --> 00:09:50.422
I went down, like,
you know, the regular way,

00:09:50.422 --> 00:09:52.791
through the be--
like, through the beginning.

00:09:52.791 --> 00:09:55.193
You know, the opening.
The beginning of a building.

00:09:55.193 --> 00:09:56.228
-Have you ever been to
the beginning of

00:09:56.228 --> 00:09:57.796
Madison Square Garden?

00:09:57.796 --> 00:10:01.233
-I got almost to the end.

00:10:01.233 --> 00:10:03.902
And I walked out the front doors
of Madison Square Garden

00:10:03.902 --> 00:10:06.304
and I walked home 13 blocks
dressed as Drunk Uncle.

00:10:06.304 --> 00:10:08.473
-Yeah. The other thing --

00:10:08.473 --> 00:10:10.743
-And they called me and they
said, "Your car is here."

00:10:10.743 --> 00:10:12.878
And I said, "I'm home."

00:10:14.212 --> 00:10:16.615
-I will say this, as well.

00:10:16.615 --> 00:10:18.016
I feel like I've done
a lot of --

00:10:18.016 --> 00:10:20.252
Like, comedy charity events
always is, like, a lower --

00:10:20.252 --> 00:10:22.087
Like, it's going to go
worse than comedy

00:10:22.087 --> 00:10:24.790
for people who pay to
see comedy -- always.

00:10:24.790 --> 00:10:26.559
But when you walk off,
more often than not,

00:10:26.559 --> 00:10:27.560
people are like,
"That was great."

00:10:27.560 --> 00:10:28.694
Like, the people
backstage are like,

00:10:28.694 --> 00:10:29.995
"We're here for a good cause."

00:10:29.995 --> 00:10:32.197
Like, the sea parted
for you and I.

00:10:32.197 --> 00:10:34.366
No one made eye contact.
It was just like...

00:10:34.366 --> 00:10:36.268
-No handler came near me.
-No, nobody.

00:10:36.268 --> 00:10:39.538
-I walked home alone.
-Yeah.

00:10:39.538 --> 00:10:41.273
People, like, would see us,
and just, with their beers,

00:10:41.273 --> 00:10:43.508
would be like, "Ooh."

00:10:43.508 --> 00:10:45.077
-I believe --
It was Katie Holmes.

00:10:45.077 --> 00:10:47.747
Katie Holmes went,
"I'm so sorry."

00:10:50.215 --> 00:10:52.051
-The other thing is that,
afterwards,

00:10:52.051 --> 00:10:53.652
do you remember,
this was a really cool thing.

00:10:53.652 --> 00:10:56.321
Because all the money
was going to Hurricane Sandy,

00:10:56.321 --> 00:10:58.323
but then they --
Half of it they gave to us

00:10:58.323 --> 00:11:01.193
because of how -- They were
like, "We want to raise money."

00:11:01.193 --> 00:11:03.462
They were like, "That was
a disaster, Hurricane Sandy,

00:11:03.462 --> 00:11:04.563
but not..."

00:11:04.563 --> 00:11:07.165
-This is a Hurricane Sandy suit.
-Oh, yeah.

00:11:07.165 --> 00:11:10.101
-This is a Hurricane Sandy suit.
They gave me this.

00:11:10.101 --> 00:11:11.470
-Well, it was an honor --

00:11:11.470 --> 00:11:13.072
It was an honor to
bomb with you that night.

00:11:13.072 --> 00:11:14.506
-If you're gonna bomb with
Seth Meyers,

00:11:14.506 --> 00:11:15.507
do it at Madison Square Garden.

00:11:15.507 --> 00:11:16.908
-Yeah, that's it.

00:11:16.908 --> 00:11:19.311
We played Madison Square --
We didn't do anything worse than

00:11:19.311 --> 00:11:22.114
the Knicks do on almost...

00:11:22.114 --> 00:11:24.083
Bobby Moynihan, everybody!

00:11:24.083 --> 00:11:27.753
"Mr. Mayor" airs Tuesday
at 8:30 p.m. here on NBC.

